'''Nur''' was a [[water]]-rich [[ocean]] [[moon]] in the [[Mustafar system]]<ref name="Art Of" /> of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Episode III" /> It was covered in [[sodium]]-rich water and had no natural land masses charted. There was also an apparent lack of indigenous sentient life, leaving the heavily secured underwater [[Fortress Inquisitorius]], as the only known structure on the moon.<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> After an [[Coruscant Incident|incident on Coruscant]],<ref name="DV20">[[Darth Vader (2017) 20|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 20]]</ref> it was used as the headquarters of the [[Inquisitorius]] and to contain captured [[Jedi]]. In [[14 BBY]], the moon and [[fortress]] were eventually [[Mission to Nur|infiltrated]] by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Cal Kestis]] and [[Cere Junda]], who were attempting to take back a [[Holocron]] stolen by the [[Second Sister]].<ref name="Jedi Fallen Order" />

In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Kenobi Date">{{KenobiDate|III}}</ref> [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]] traveled to Nur from [[Daiyu]] and, on orders from [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], launched three probes to help aid in the search of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]. After one located him on [[Mapuzo]], Third Sister, [[Fifth Brother]], and [[Fourth Sister]] joined Vader on the planet to capture him.<ref name="K3">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref> Later that same year, Princess [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] was kidnapped by Third Sister and taken to Nur. [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Tala Durith]] infiltrated the moon to rescue the princess. The duo succeeded and escaped with the help of [[Wade Resselian|Wade]] and [[Sully Stark|Sully]].<ref name="K4">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref>

{{Moon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[Star Wars Inside Intel|''Star Wars Inside Intel: The Inquisitorius'']] stated that Nur orbited<ref name="Insider Intel old">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-inside-intel-the-inquisitorius|text=''Star Wars'' Inside Intel: The Inquisitorius|int=Star Wars Inside Intel}} {{C|version archived on Janurary 20, 2023; content now replaced}}</ref> the [[planet]]<ref name="Episode III" /> [[Mustafar]].<ref name="Insider Intel old" /> However, this was later edited in [[2023]] to more vaguely state it was part of the Mustafar system.<ref name="Insider Intel">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-inside-intel-the-inquisitorius|text=''Star Wars'' Inside Intel: The Inquisitorius|int=Star Wars Inside Intel}}</ref> Later that year,<ref name="DK UK">{{DK|url=uk/book/9780241666371-star-wars-dawn-of-rebellion-the-visual-guide|text=Star Wars Dawn of Rebellion The Visual Guide}}</ref> ''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' would once again place Nur as orbiting Mustafar.<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> However, the episode "[[Devoted]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Tales of the Empire]]'' shows Nur orbiting<ref name="Devoted" /> the planet<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'', 2016 edition]]</ref> [[Jestefad]], with Mustafar visible in the background.<ref name="Devoted" /> This is supported by a hologram in "[[Part IV]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' showing Nur's orbit around a planet that is not Mustafar.<ref name="K4" />

